      {
        "ref": "1SA1:3",
        "textualBasisJa": "This man went up out of his city from year to year to worship and to sacrifice to the LORD of Armies in Shiloh. The two sons of Eli, Hophni and Phinehas, priests to the LORD, were there."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA2:34",
        "textualBasisJa": "This will be the sign to you that will come on your two sons, on Hophni and Phinehas: in one day they will both die."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA4:4",
        "textualBasisJa": "So the people sent to Shiloh, and they brought from there the ark of the covenant of the LORD of Armies, who sits above the cherubim; and the two sons of Eli, Hophni and Phinehas, were there with the ark of the covenant of God."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA4:11",
        "textualBasisJa": "God’s ark was taken; and the two sons of Eli, Hophni and Phinehas, were slain."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA4:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "He who brought the news answered, “Israel has fled before the Philistines, and there has been also a great slaughter among the people. Your two sons also, Hophni and Phinehas, are dead, and God’s ark has been captured.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA14:3",
        "textualBasisJa": "including Ahijah the son of Ahitub, Ichabod’s brother, the son of Phinehas, the son of Eli the priest of the LORD in Shiloh, wearing an ephod. The people didn’t know that Jonathan was gone."
      },
